{
  "_comment": [
    "Trusted file-identity manifest for the linecast backend this plugin",
    "is reviewed against. Generated once from the official PyPI release",
    "(never from an installed environment's own RECORD, which an",
    "unpinned/attacker-controlled install could self-report anything into)",
    "-- see README.md -> Security -> Backend binding, and",
    "resolve_verified_linecast() in ptyrun.py, which is the only thing",
    "that reads this file.",
    "",
    "Pinned to 2.3.1 rather than a later release: linecast 2.4.0 changed",
    "every --live view's redraw strategy to absolute per-row cursor",
    "addressing (ESC[row;colH) with no plain newlines at all, which this",
    "plugin's renderer (Ansi.js -- a simple append-until-newline parser",
    "with no real 2D grid model -- and Quickshell's own newline-keyed",
    "SplitParser) cannot display at all (every tab shows \"No data\").",
    "2.3.1 is the last release using the newline-streamed rendering this",
    "plugin actually understands. See",
    "github.com/JMThomas00/omarchy-linecast/issues/5 for the tracked",
    "follow-up to properly support newer releases."
  ],
